Consider an internal vertex $v \in T - \mathcal{L}$ with children $u_{1}, u_{2}$.
The design of $\mathcal{A}$ ensures that:
\begin{DenseEnumerate}

\item \label{item:independence}
the random variable
$\mathbf{1}(v \in \mathit{D}(t))$
is independent of the coin tosses of all vertices $u \in T(v)$ (including
$v$);

\item \label{item:match-on-top}
$\mathcal{A}$ can match on top of $v$ only when $v$ is odd; and

\item \label{item:match-across}
if $\mathcal{A}$ matched across or on top of $v$ at time $t$, then

$v$, $u_{1}$, and $u_{2}$ are not odd immediately following time
$t$, i.e.,

$v, u_{1}, u_{2} \notin \mathit{D}(t + d t)$
for infinitesimally small
$d t > 0$.

\end{DenseEnumerate}

